 back with myself\" — see the 2023-10-23 entry of ## Relationships; complements the childhood memories of tinkering with engines in his dad's garage recorded above; Calvin: \"Impressive! That must have taken a lot of skill and determination to bring that car back to life.\", and asked whether it was a classic car and whether Dave still has it or is working on another project — Dave answered in the continuation of the same day's chat, which is not in this excerpt: he restored a car last year (2022, the 2022 restoration, see above) but sold it to a collector, and is now working on a new car project he finds quite a challenge [S25T14][S25T15][S25T16][S25T17].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin (who asked what the toughest part of car restoration is) that it takes a lot of patience but the payoff is worth it, and paying extra attention to detail isn't easy but it pays off — echoing his earlier remarks that small details make his mod project unique and personalized (details in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) and that the small successes make him proud (see above) [S25T18][S25T19].\n- On 2023-10-25, said working on a car project \"takes me out of my head and calms me down\" — complementing his long-stated \"oasis of calm\"/therapy remarks above [S26T4].\n- As of 2023-10-29, is also getting into photography (a new hobby — details and the Boston photos he shared are in the Photography section below) [S27T2][S27T8].","text_sha256":"77806b5cdf089784b714c24e9ae79301aca4f68b7a768af55fd0856103bf2a0d","timestamp":null}],"integrity":{"post_tree_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","pre_tree_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","store_unchanged":true,"verified":true},"metrics":{"completion_tokens":654,"filesystem_tool_calls":0,"model_calls":4,"orchestration_calls":4,"prompt_tokens":50281,"provider_request_attempts":4,"provider_rounds":4,"token_usage_available":true,"total_tokens":50935},"model":{"requested_mod